@MrSummitville Yes, a ceasefire was announced in April. U.S. strikes continued afterward. CENTCOM itself confirmed that American aircraft struck Iranian missile, drone, and radar sites on June 26. AP has now reported further U.S. strikes on November 2, described by a U.S. official as defensive.

A ground invasion is not required for air and naval hostilities. And yes, U.S. operations have helped ships get through Hormuz—but the November 1 maritime advisory also rated the threat severe and estimated around 490 vessels waiting outside.

Some oil moving and some ships getting through are compatible with an ongoing conflict. Whether the strategy is working is a separate argument. “What war?” does not account for the documented military action.
